{"name":"Chicory Coffee","hex":"#4d3730","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chicory coffee","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A drink, resembling coffee, made from the roasted roots of chicory"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chicory_coffee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chicory","blocks":[{"text":"Common chicory is a somewhat woody, perennial herbaceous plant of the family Asteraceae, usually with bright blue flowers, rarely white or pink. Native to Europe, North Africa, and western Asia, it has been introduced to the Americas, Australia, and South Africa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Illustration_Cichorium_intybus0_clean.jpg/330px-Illustration_Cichorium_intybus0_clean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicory"},{"title":"Coffee","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a beverage brewed from roasted, ground coffee beans. Dark-colored and bitter, coffee has a stimulating effect on humans due to its caffeine content; however decaffeinated coffee is also commercially available. There are also various coffee substitutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg/330px-Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee"},{"title":"Coffee (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a brownish color that is a representation of a roasted coffee bean. Different types of coffee beans have different colors when roasted—the color coffee represents an average."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Wegwarte_Cichorium